---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Editorial Policy — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"How this publication tests, sources, discloses and corrects — including its position on AI assistance."}
  canonicalPath={"/about/editorial-policy/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .pg-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .pg-head h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .pg-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 58ch; }
  .pg-head--dark { background: var(--dark); color: var(--dark-text); padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .pg-head--dark .crumbs { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .pg-head--dark .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--dark-text); }
  .pg-head--dark .lede { color: var(--dark-muted); }

  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose > * + * { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.016em; margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 3.75rem); }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; letter-spacing: -0.012em; }
  .prose p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .prose a:not(.link):not(.btn) { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .rule-list li {
    padding-block: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.75rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .rule-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .rule-list li::before {
    content: ""; inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: transparent; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong); margin-top: 0.62rem;
  }
  .rule-list strong { color: var(--ink); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }

  .callout { border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.5rem; }
  .callout strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .callout p { color: var(--ink); }

  .facts { display: grid; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--dark-line); margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .facts > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 12rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; padding-block: 0.875rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--dark-line-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .facts dt { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .facts dd { color: var(--dark-text); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.1875rem; } }

  .timeline { position: relative; padding-left: 2rem; }
  .timeline::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 3px; top: 1.2rem; bottom: 1.2rem; width: 1px; background: var(--line-strong); }
  .timeline li { position: relative; padding-block: 1.125rem; }
  .timeline li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -2rem; top: 1.7rem;
    inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--canvas); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li:last-child::before { background: var(--ember-bright); box-shadow: none; }
  .timeline time { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .timeline h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; letter-spacing: -0.011em; margin: 0 0 0.375rem; }
  .timeline p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }

  .listing li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.375rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.375rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .listing a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .listing h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.014em; }
  .listing p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 58ch; }
  .listing__tail { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .listing a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 16rem) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 9rem); align-items: start; }
    .listing__tail { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  }

  .glossary > div { padding-block: 1.125rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary dt { font-weight: 550; font-size: 1.0625rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .glossary dd { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 0.25rem; max-width: 60ch; }

  .sources { margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sources h2 { font-size: var(--t-h3); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .sources ol { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; counter-reset: src; }
  .sources li { counter-increment: src; padding-left: 2rem; position: relative; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
  .sources li::before { content: counter(src); position: absolute; left: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); }
  .sources a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="pg-head" data-od-id="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/about/">About</a></li>
          <li>Editorial policy</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      
      <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">How pages here are researched, tested, sourced and corrected — written down so it can be held against us.</p>
      
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="band" data-od-id="policy-body">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What every page must contain</h2>
        <p>
          A page is not published unless it delivers at least one of the following:
          a workflow you can reproduce, a test you can follow, original screenshots or
          audio, a specific problem solved, a properly researched historical account, or
          a resource list that has been checked and dated.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing here exists to occupy a search term. If a page cannot meet that bar,
          it does not get written.
        </p>

        <h2>Testing and versions</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><div><strong>Version and date are stated</strong>Technical articles name the software version, operating system and test date. A guide with no date is a guide with no value.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Untested is labelled untested</strong>Where something was researched rather than run, the page says so plainly instead of implying first-hand experience.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Failures stay in</strong>Where a method broke, the article documents the break and the fix. Removing them makes for a cleaner read and a less useful one.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Screenshots are ours</strong>Interface images come from the machine the article was written on, at the stated version.</div></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Sources</h2>
        <p>
          Factual claims are sourced, preferring primary documentation over secondary
          coverage. Where a figure comes from a manufacturer or a platform, it is dated,
          because those figures change. Where something is convention rather than fact —
          a starting point for a reverb decay, for instance — it is described as such.
        </p>

        <h2>AI assistance</h2>
        <p>
          Language tools are used in production here, for drafting structure, editing and
          checking. They are not used to generate technical claims, and no page is
          published on the strength of a model's assertion about how a piece of software
          behaves. Anything technical is verified against the software itself or against
          primary documentation.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            <strong>No page is published as generated text.</strong>
            Every article passes through a human who is answerable for its claims. If a
            claim here is wrong, it is a person's error, not a tool's.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Commercial relationships</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><div><strong>Disclosure is on the page</strong>Any commercial relationship relevant to an article is stated in the article, not buried in a policy page.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>One commercial link at most</strong>An article carries no more than one primary commercial link, and only where it genuinely serves the reader.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>No article exists for a link</strong>If removing the link would leave nothing worth publishing, the page should not exist.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>No paid placement in reviews</strong>Review verdicts are not for sale, and equipment received for testing would be disclosed as such.</div></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Errors are corrected on the page, with the change recorded and dated rather than
          quietly overwritten. Substantial corrections are noted at the point of the
          correction. Historical and attribution errors are treated as urgent.
        </p>

        <h2>What this publication will not do</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><div><strong>Invent authors, reviews or testimonials</strong>Every name on this site belongs to a real person.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Invent metrics</strong>No unsourced performance claims, no fabricated popularity figures, no star ratings without a stated method.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Redistribute work it has no right to</strong>Including anything published by the former operator of this domain.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Backdate a publication date</strong>Historical context is shown as historical context, never as a current publication date.</div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="relaunch-notice">
    <div class="shell relaunch">
      <p>Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026. Historical
         references are preserved for context.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">Read the history and relaunch note
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>